From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:50:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: fold the station configuration and remove test
 surface

Experiment candidate for the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 1, not for
upstream. It is a checkpoint: the clean series will replace the station's
Wi-Fi patches once this behaves like them.

Resolve the 48 Kconfig switches to the station's values in the source.
Fixed MCS5 (0x85), transmit depth 12, a status report on 1 frame in 64,
HT40, receive A-MPDU and the polled, batched and peeked receive path are
now the code, not options. Then remove what only served measurement:
- the snapshot facility;
- the per-association test configuration and its schedule, so that
  every association uses the build configuration (association 1 of the
  station already did), together with the SGI path only it could
  enable;
- the dead branches left by the fold, including the unstable-epoch arms,
  the native monitor command and the unreachable per-port PIO receive
  tail;
- the pass-cost, rate and data-phase records and the end-of-data log
  burst;
- the CONSYS WMT query, identity and Bluetooth reset modes and their
  headers, the region19 snapshot, the alias attributes and hex dumps.

Add a rate_control module parameter. Off (the default) keeps the fixed
rate; on uses mac80211's minstrel. It is read once per association.

The native-delivery state machine stays, because it carries the CCMP
receive path. Every kernel message the station's wifi-cycles.sh matches
is unchanged. The start attributes are unchanged too: region19_prepare,
wmt_negotiate and wlan_stop.

Compile-tested with W=1; not yet run on hardware.
